# The real noindex/noimageindex control for /demo, /verify and /admin — not
# src/hooks/use-noindex.ts.
#
# `index.html`'s old blanket `<meta name="robots" content="noindex">` covered
# every route in the one static document Workers static assets serves for
# all of them. M20 plan §A4 made `/` indexable, which meant that tag could no
# longer live in the shared shell at all. A React-injected <meta> tag
# (use-noindex.ts) only exists after the bundle has loaded and run — a
# crawler that does not execute JavaScript never sees it.
#
# This file is read by Cloudflare Workers static assets (same format as
# Pages' `_headers`) and applies to *asset* responses only — never to
# responses your own Worker code generates. That is exactly right here:
# apps/api/wrangler.toml's `run_worker_first` covers only `/api/*`,
# `/health` and `/openapi.json`, so `/demo`, `/verify` and everything under
# `/admin` are asset responses, resolved by the [assets] binding before any
# Worker code runs, and this file's rules apply to them.
#
# CONFIRMED AGAINST PRODUCTION 2026-08-21: `_headers` path matching is on the
# *original* incoming request path, not the SPA-rewritten one —
# `not_found_handling = "single-page-application"` serves `/index.html`'s
# bytes for an unmatched path, but the header rule still keyed off what the
# browser actually requested:
#
#   /verify          → x-robots-tag: noindex     (rule applied)
#   /admin/dashboard → x-robots-tag: noindex     (rule applied)
#   /                → absent                    (correctly not matched)
#
# That is the standard, documented use of `_headers` for SPA routes
# elsewhere in Cloudflare's ecosystem, and it is now settled rather than
# assumed — no `run_worker_first` fallback is needed.
#
# `use-noindex.ts` stays wired into `/admin` and `/contribute` regardless:
# defense in depth for crawlers that do execute JavaScript, not the primary
# control. `/demo` does not call it (M24, plan §B2) — see that page's own
# comment and `CONTEXT.md` §Q25's amendment for why dropping the page-level
# `noindex` there is not the same as dropping the bound it used to carry.
#
# Rules may contain only a single splat (`*`) each.

# M24, plan §B2: `/demo` (renamed from `/verify`) is indexable — the page,
# not the frames. `noimageindex` keeps Googlebot's own image cache (which
# outlives a frame's short-lived signed URL, and is the actual path by which
# a copyrighted frame could reach image search) out of image search while
# leaving the page itself discoverable and shareable.
/demo
  X-Robots-Tag: noimageindex

# The old path, kept working as a redirect (`routes.tsx`) rather than
# deleted — it is linked from the landing page's own history, this repo's
# docs, and anywhere a stranger already pasted the old URL. `noindex`, not
# `noimageindex`: this path now serves nothing but a client-side redirect,
# and a crawler that does not execute JavaScript would otherwise index a
# blank shell as if it were its own page.
/verify
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex

/admin
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex

/admin/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
